From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:02:38 +0100
Subject: [regexp] Don't share results cache entries with captures across
 realms

The REGEXP_MULTIPLE_INDICES results cache is per isolate and keyed on
the subject and the RegExpDataWrapper, both of which are shared across
native contexts. But for patterns with named captures, the entry
contains groups objects specific to a native context, and a cache hit
clones them together with their maps. A replace callback in another
native context was thus passed objects from the wrong native context.

On a hit for a pattern with captures, check that the cached argument
arrays were created in the current native context, and treat a mismatch
as a miss.

Fixed: 576225189
Change-Id: Ib0310916b3881c40772bbff8544d2ffae2b98074
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8653980
Reviewed-by: Patrick Thier <pthier@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Patrick Thier <pthier@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111136}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
runtime-regexp.cc: the 3-way merge left this branch's old cache-hit block
(plain CopyFixedArrayWithMap + SetLastMatchInfo) next to the new guarded
block; the old block is removed so the function matches upstream. No
semantic change.
runtime-regexp.cc: in the cache-hit block re_data is not yet declared on
this branch, so the capture-name-map check uses
TrustedCast<IrRegExpData>(regexp_data) directly (has_capture guards it).

